[[File:E 167.png|thumb|[[Shibalien|Shibalien]], the first example of an Alien enemy]]
'''Alien Enemies''' (エイリアン ''Eirian'') are a type of [[Enemy Units|Enemy Unit]] introduced in Chapter 1 of [[Into the Future]]. These cyan enemies are rather strong, generally don't give much money, and come in two varieties: [[:Category:Unstarred Alien Enemies|unstarred]] and [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred]]. They have a knack for causing status effects, from debuffs or buffs to themselves, making them ideal targets to be [[Curse|Cursed]]. Many enemies with this trait tend to act as backliners.

Aliens' health and damage are initially multiplied by either 700% for unstarred Aliens or 1,600% for Starred Aliens depending on their subtype, making them EXTREMELY strong initially. This is especially the case when combined with the buffs in stages such as [[Honey Trap (Deadly)|Queen's Coronation]] and [[Puffer Planet (Merciless)|Blue Impact]], rendering them almost unbeatable without at least some of the anti-Alien crystal [[Treasure]]s. Each 100% Treasure reduces this multiplier by 100% (66% reduces it by 66%, 33% by 33%, and so on).

Unstarred Aliens and Starred Aliens each have their own debuffing Treasures; Treasures debuffing one subtype will not debuff the other. For more information, see [[Anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]] and [[Anti-Starred Alien Treasures]].

See [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|here]] for a list of units with anti-Alien abilities.

*The [[Ototo Corps|Breakerblast Foundation]] reduces the damage all [[Cat Units]] take from Alien enemies by 0.75% per level up to a maximum of 15%.
*Alien enemies are associated with Blue [[Catfruit]], which can be obtained from the [[Growing Catfruit]] stage [[Blue Illusion]].
*Anti-Alien abilities are improved by the [[Enigma Fruit]] from [[Cats of the Cosmos]].
*Alien [[Talent Orbs]] can be obtained from the following stages:
**[[Enigma Stages]]: [[Cradle Shrine (Deadly)/Alien|Cosmic Cradle]], [[Summit Shrine (Merciless)/Alien|Cosmic Summit]], [[Frontier Shrine (Merciless)/Alien|Cosmic Frontier]]
**[[Island of Hidden Treasure]]: [[Azure Dawn]], [[Azure Apex]], [[Azure Refuge]]
**[[Horrorpotamus]] [[Continuation Stage]]s: [[Horrorpotamus/Cradle Wilderness (Deadly)|Cradle Wilderness]], [[Horrorpotamus/Summit Wilderness (Merciless)|Summit Wilderness]], [[Horrorpotamus/Frontier Wilderness (Merciless)|Frontier Wilderness]]

==Trivia==
*Several Aliens have a lump known only as "THAT" (アレ ''Are''), described as a sign of Alien control in the [[Into the Future/OPEDJP|Japanese Into the Future opening]], growing from their heads, including [[Hyppoh]], [[Cyberhorn]], [[Galactic Overseer Nyandam]], [[Le'Solar]], [[Satan Claus]], [[Super Hyppoh]] and Into the Future's narrator, who claims to have eight of THAT. [[Helmut Krabbe]] is also stated to have THAT growing from his rear, and [[Bun Bun Symbiote]]'s Japanese description mentions the proliferation/multiplication of THAT.
*Some of [[Into the Future]]'s [[Enemy Bases|enemy bases]] feature Aliens that cannot be fought as actual enemies, such as [[Germany (Into the Future)|Germany]]'s and [[Nepal (Into the Future)|Nepal]]'s.
*Several Aliens appear to reference ''[[wikipedia:Ultraman|Ultraman]]'':
**[[Scissoroo]] references [[wikia:ultra:Alien Baltan|Alien Baltan]], a lobster-ish alien with similar metal pincers. Scissoroo uses blasters hidden inside her pincers to attack, just like how Alien Baltans have various hidden weapons inside their pincers.
**[[Shibalien Elite]]'s crest/fin/mohawk is likely a reference to that of [[wikia:Ultra:Ultraseven (character)|Ultraseven]], which looks almost the same when viewed from the side.
**[[Star Peng]] is likely a reference to [[wikia:ultra:Bemstar|Bemstar]], as both are avian extraterrestrials with the word "star" in their name, a horn-like protrusion on their head and a pentagon-in-a-pentagon on their belly.
**[[Le'Solar]]'s pigtail-like protrusions resemble [[wikia:ultra:Mother of Ultra|Mother of Ultra]]'s Silver Cross Decorations. Both characters' Japanese names also contain ''haha'' (meaning "mother"), with Le'Solar being Haha Paon (ハハパオン, "Mother [[Le'boin|Paon]]") and Mother of Ultra being Ultra no Haha (ウルトラの母).
**[[Youcan]] strongly resembles [[wikia:ultra:Alien Guts|Alien Guts]], though with the proportions of an actual bird and a larger beak in exchange for reduced brain volume.
**[[UltraBaaBaa]]'s design could be a reference to [[wikia:ultra:Pigmon|Pigmon]], a similarly spiky kaiju. Some portrayals of Pigmon give his spikes a texture rather like the ones on UltraBaaBaa's head, and both have grooves in their legs and tail. Her tail is also noticeably longer than [[Baa Baa]]'s (its full length can be seen right when she attacks), bringing it closer to Pigmon's. 
*[[Project A]] is the only Alien enemy whose Japanese name is written entirely in kanji.
*[[Doge]], [[Gory]] and the [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclone]]s are the only enemies to have both unstarred and Starred Alien variants.
*There is an Alien variant of every [[Empire of Cats]] enemy except [[Snache]], [[Those Guys]], [[B.B.Bunny]], [[Squire Rel]] and [[Ms. Sign]].

